  "invariants": [
    "Entity identity is independent of model, provider, channel, session, process and workflow.",
    "Root Constitution v1.0 and canonical Entity DNA v1.2 remain unchanged in this candidate.",
    "Only Registry, Event and State records may constitute canonical operational truth.",
    "Every model, council and shadow result is proposal-only and has zero inherent authority.",
    "No fallback may reduce minimum Resolution, policy, authority, evidence or data-class constraints.",
    "Up-resolution reloads canonical state and never reconstructs fields omitted by a lower projection.",
    "Fractal expansion is local, trigger-driven, depth-bounded, attempt-bounded and budget-bounded.",
    "Every model sees only an allowlisted projection bound to an exact profile version and hash.",
    "Provider switching preserves the request, pack, projection, policy and output-contract bindings.",
    "Structured decisions are normalized before deterministic rendering and semantic comparison.",
    "External effects require Policy pass, exact ApprovalBinding and an idempotent Outbox intent.",
    "Approval is bound to the exact normalized intent hash and cannot authorize a changed effect.",
    "Shadow learning cannot mutate production behavior directly and promotion is one maturity step at a time.",
    "C5 promotion requires Human Root approval and C6 additionally requires verified restore evidence.",
